# Try the API from inside VS Code.
# Install the "REST Client" extension (by Huachao Mao), start the server (python app.py),
# then click "Send Request" above any request below. Go top to bottom for the full story.

@base = http://localhost:5000/api

### 0. Is the server up?
GET {{base}}/health

### 1. A resident gives a missed call (creates a ticket)
POST {{base}}/webhooks/missed-call
Content-Type: application/json

{ "from": "9800000001" }

### 2. Same resident calls again (returns the SAME ticket, no duplicate)
POST {{base}}/webhooks/missed-call
Content-Type: application/json

{ "from": "9800000001" }

### 3. A number that is not registered
POST {{base}}/webhooks/missed-call
Content-Type: application/json

{ "from": "9899999999" }

### 4. Another household requests from the app/website (the "Request a pickup" form)
POST {{base}}/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{ "gate_id": "KTM-W10-0043", "waste_type": "green" }

### 5. See the open requests (what a collector sees)
GET {{base}}/requests?status=requested

### 6. Dispatch ticket 1 to collector 1
POST {{base}}/requests/1/assign
Content-Type: application/json

{ "collector_id": 1 }

### 7. Collector's queue
GET {{base}}/collectors/1/queue

### 8. Wrong QR scanned (rejected)
POST {{base}}/requests/1/collect
Content-Type: application/json

{ "scanned_gate_id": "KTM-W10-0043", "collector_id": 1, "segregation_verified": true }

### 9. Right QR, segregation verified (saves the event and awards Green Points)
POST {{base}}/requests/1/collect
Content-Type: application/json

{ "scanned_gate_id": "KTM-W10-0042", "collector_id": 1, "segregation_verified": true, "notes": "Bins were sorted" }

### 10. Household summary with Green Points
GET {{base}}/households/KTM-W10-0042

### 11. Points history
GET {{base}}/households/KTM-W10-0042/points

### 12. All collection events
GET {{base}}/collections

### 13. Cancel a request
POST {{base}}/requests/2/cancel

### 14. Register a new household (gets its gate ID automatically)
POST {{base}}/households
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Maya Karki", "phone": "9841234567", "ward": 10, "address": "New Baneshwor" }
